Feature: G8, K on the GPU: the frame path stays on the GPU from decoded clip to encoder
  The UGC edit (738 frames, 1080x1920, 30 fps: Buddy's take cut on sentences, captions, two b-rolls, a ducked music
  bed) rendered, previewed and scrubbed through K kernels on GPU-resident data. M4 Mac, 2026-10-14. Raw numbers in
  bench/; the kernels are raea-kgpu/kernels/*.k (K, compiled to WGSL by raea-kgpu, generated by kernels/gen.py).

  Background:
    Given step 0 finished G7 first: the bake-off report is ../media/docs/bakeoff.feature, the licence record
      ../media/docs/licences.feature, the Linux container run ../media/bench/linux-container.txt, the
      playback checks bench/playback.jsonl, the reference hashes examples/out/ref/hash-*.txt
    And step 0 is the reference: RAEA_READBACK=rgba renders through it unchanged (clips and the overlay as Bevy UI
      nodes, an RGBA readback), and still reproduces its 738 hashes

